WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.250
She quits social media:
«Elle a décidé de quitter

2
00:00:03.250 --> 00:00:05.350
les réseaux sociaux.» Word for word,

3
00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:07.880
she decided 'of' leaving.

4
00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:10.750
He wins the argument:
«Il a réussi à convaincre

5
00:00:10.750 --> 00:00:14.250
ses parents.» He succeeded
'at' convincing them.

6
00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:18.670
And hope? «J'espère trouver un
emploi.» No little word at all.

7
00:00:18.670 --> 00:00:21.910
English says 'to' almost every time.

8
00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:23.870
So when is it «à»,

9
00:00:23.870 --> 00:00:27.700
when is it «de», and when
is it nothing at all?

10
00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:30.340
In this mission, you'll draw
the boot round irregular

11
00:00:30.340 --> 00:00:33.740
verbs in Mission D1, like «venir».

12
00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:36.970
Then you'll build sentences in Mission I1,

13
00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:40.500
choosing your pronoun and
your little word each time.

14
00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:45.750
Your mission: work out how the
French choose between «à» and «de»,

15
00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:47.310
and how you can too.
